and are not subject to copyright in the United States (17 U.S.C. § 105). They
are not ours to license and we make no claim over them.

Caveat: a federal release can contain third-party material — a contractor's
report, a press clipping, a photograph taken by someone outside government —
that carries its own rights. Public domain applies to the government's own
work, not automatically to everything reproduced inside a government file.

