Note on the choice. CC0 would place the spine in the public domain and remove
the attribution requirement. That was considered and rejected, because the
stated goal is that researchers cite the corpus rather than reuse it silently.
Switching to CC0 is a one-file change if that goal changes — but it cannot be
un-done for copies already distributed under it, so it is worth deciding once.

This is a starting point drafted by a maintainer, not legal advice.
